    "sourceWikitext": "{{recipesummary|category=Taro recipes|servings=4 persons|time=20 minutes|difficulty=3}}{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of China|Chinese Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian]]\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* 1 small [[Cookbook:Taro Root|taro]]\n* 2 sheets [[Cookbook:Nori|nori]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] preserved black beans\n* 2-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] piece of [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 1 green pepper\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Spring Onion|spring onions]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] vegetable [[Cookbook:Dehydrated Broth|stock powder]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] Shaoxing rice [[Cookbook:Wine|wine]]\n* [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|Vegetable oil]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Peel and [[Cookbook:Chopping|chop]] taro into 1-inch chunks. Steam until soft.\n# Meanwhile soak black beans in a little water. \n# Mash taro with the vegetable stock powder. \n# Place 2 sheets of nori on the bench, moistening one to join them together.\n# Place the mashed taro mixture in the centre of the sheets and roll the nori sheets over the top.  \n# Cut the nori at one end to resemble fish fins.  \n# Slice green pepper, ginger and spring onions into thin strips and [[Cookbook:Stir-frying|stir fry]] for a few minutes.  \n# Add the Shaoxing wine and black beans.\n# Make cuts halfway through the taro fish at about 1 inch intervals and pour the sauce over it.  \n# Serve on a platter.\n\n[[Category:Chinese recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using taro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using seaweed]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]",
    "isRecipe": true,
